{:frontmatter
 {:id "adr-2607120730-yoro-social-fold-scaling-incremental-fold-design"
  :title "ADR-2607120730: yoro-social-v2 fold does not scale (full-rebuild, no incremental prolly-tree insert) -- incremental-fold design, periodic kawaraban/media writes paused"
  :status "accepted"
  :doc_type "adr"
  :topic "kotobase-scaling"
  :authoritative true
  :last_verified "2026-07-12"
  :authoritative_for
  ["kotobase-peer.core/fold! is an O(total shared-graph size) full rebuild, not an
    incremental update -- prolly-tree.core exposes only build-tree/lookup/scan-prefix,
    no incremental insert primitive exists anywhere in the stack today"
   "yoro-social-v2 is the shared cross-actor AppView index (YORO_DB_NAME), not
    kawaraban's own graph -- its total size grows with the whole aozora ecosystem's
    history, not with any single actor's write volume, so no amount of throttling one
    actor's writes alone bounds fold's cost"
   "the originally-requested periodic execution wiring (GitHub Actions cron for
    kawaraban live-ingest and cloud-itonami media-digest) is PAUSED, not abandoned,
    pending this fix -- further scheduled writes against an already-unrecoverable
    backlog would only make the eventual fix harder"
   "no data was lost -- the problem is read latency/availability against unfolded
    novelty, not durability (writes are append-only content-addressed R2 objects
    regardless of fold status)"]
  :supersedes []
  :superseded_by []
  :related ["orgs/kotoba-lang/kotobase-peer/src/kotobase_peer/core.cljc"
            "orgs/kotoba-lang/arrangement/src/arrangement/core.cljc"
            "orgs/kotoba-lang/prolly-tree/src/prolly_tree/core.cljc"
